Pipeline operations for npm-based client-side web application projects.
Shell scripts in ../code/ serve as the central entrypoints for critical commands:
   - compile.sh → build invocation (used by build_op)
   - test.sh    → test invocation (used by test_run_op)
   - install.sh → dependency installation (used by install_op)
These scripts must NOT be bypassed or modified to work around errors.
They provide platform routing flexibility with consistent error handling.


Recommended execution order:
1. design_op    - Capture technology and architecture decisions
2. scaffold_op  - Generate project skeleton and configs
3. install_op   - Run install.sh (dependency installation)
4. implement_op - Write application source code
5. test_write_op - Write test files
6. build_op     - Run compile.sh (with auto-fix)
7. test_run_op  - Run test.sh (with auto-fix)
8. update_op    - Apply iterative changes from user notes